# The documentation's diagrams (components/docs/diagrams)
dg-figure = Figure { $n }

dg-map-caption = One agent, reachable from anywhere, and a journal of everything it does. The core knows no vendor: the rest are adapters.
dg-map-reach = People reach it through
dg-map-satellites = Satellites
dg-map-satellites-note = Speakers, robots, screens, a browser tab. In writing, aloud or both.
dg-map-telegram = Telegram
dg-map-telegram-note = In writing, from anywhere.
dg-map-more = WhatsApp, Signal, Matrix
dg-map-more-note = Other messaging services, same contract.
dg-map-core = The core
dg-map-agent = The conversation agent
dg-map-agent-note = A fast model per medium, direct tools, streamed answers.
dg-map-memory = Memory
dg-map-memory-note = What it was told, and what each past conversation was about.
dg-map-initiative = Initiative
dg-map-initiative-note = Wake-ups, watches, messages, and the courier that delivers them.
dg-map-tasks = Tasks
dg-map-tasks-note = Long work handed to an executor, followed to the end.
dg-map-home = Household
dg-map-home-note = People, rooms, presence, quiet hours.
dg-map-plugged = Plugged in
dg-map-models = Models
dg-map-models-note = Profiles you name, used by role. Any OpenAI-compatible API, cloud or local.
dg-map-ha = Home Assistant
dg-map-ha-note = Devices, rooms, who is home.
dg-map-connectors = Connectors
dg-map-connectors-note = Google, Microsoft 365, CalDAV, IMAP, any MCP server.
dg-map-executors = Executors
dg-map-executors-note = Hermes, for research and paperwork.
dg-map-journal = The journal
dg-map-journal-note = Every turn, tool call, memory, message and decision, as events in one SQLite file. The admin reads it; a restart rebuilds from it.

dg-turn-caption = A turn, from message to answer. On the right, the events journaled at each step.
dg-turn-steps = What happens
dg-turn-journal = What the journal records
dg-turn-arrives = A message arrives
dg-turn-arrives-note = Said to a satellite or typed in Telegram. The account tells Nestor who speaks, when it knows.
dg-turn-joins = It joins a conversation
dg-turn-joins-note = Turns close in time form one: five minutes aloud, four hours in writing, by default. Each event carries its id.
dg-turn-builds = The instructions are built
dg-turn-builds-note = In layers, most stable first, so the provider's cache keeps most of them.
dg-turn-acts = The model answers and acts
dg-turn-acts-note = It streams its answer and calls tools: home, memory, wake-ups, messages, tasks.
dg-turn-answers = The answer goes back the way it came
dg-turn-answers-note = Spoken or written. If interrupted, only what was heard is kept.
dg-turn-delegates = Long work leaves the conversation
dg-turn-delegates-note = Research or paperwork becomes an executor's task. Its result is announced once, even after a restart.

dg-layers-caption = A turn's instructions, most stable first. Everything before a cache point is read from the cache: a new turn pays in full only for what changed.
dg-layers-stable = Stable
dg-layers-stable-note = Who it is, its rules, its tools, the executors it can call.
dg-layers-stable-pace = changes with the configuration
dg-layers-household = Household
dg-layers-household-note = Memories, watches, wake-ups.
dg-layers-household-pace = changes now and then
dg-layers-turn = Turn
dg-layers-turn-note = The time, who speaks, what their words find in memory and past conversations, open questions, running tasks.
dg-layers-turn-pace = changes every turn
dg-layers-conversation = Conversation
dg-layers-conversation-note = The open conversation's turns, with their tool calls.
dg-layers-conversation-pace = grows with each turn
dg-layers-point = cache point
dg-layers-cached = read from the cache

dg-memory-caption = Where a turn's memory comes from: the latest memories in the cached household layer, what the speaker's words find in the turn layer, the rest through tools.
dg-memory-memories = Memories
dg-memory-memories-note = Lasting facts and preferences, dated, about someone or the household.
dg-memory-episodes = Episodes
dg-memory-episodes-note = One per past conversation, seen only by its participants.
dg-memory-journal = The journal
dg-memory-journal-note = Every word, as said and heard.
dg-memory-into-household = Household layer, cached
dg-memory-into-turn = Turn layer, for whoever speaks
dg-memory-into-tools = On demand, through tools
dg-memory-memories-latest = The latest 150 memories
dg-memory-memories-found = Beyond them, up to 12 the words find
dg-memory-episodes-recent = Their 3 latest conversations
dg-memory-episodes-older = Up to 4 older ones the words find
dg-memory-memories-recall = recall finds memories by words and meaning
dg-memory-episodes-recall = recall finds conversations, between two dates if asked
dg-memory-journal-reread = read_conversation rereads one, word for word

dg-search-caption = By words, the choir comes first: it shares two words with the question. By meaning, the diet does. Fused, the memory in both lists leads. Without an embedding model, words alone.
dg-search-question-label = Hugo asks
dg-search-question = What can I cook for Léa this evening?
dg-search-words = By words (FTS5, BM25)
dg-search-meaning = By meaning (embeddings)
dg-search-fused = Fused by reciprocal rank
dg-search-memory-choir = Léa has choir practice every Tuesday evening.
dg-search-memory-vegetarian = Léa is vegetarian.
dg-search-memory-coriander = Hugo cannot stand coriander.

dg-consolidation-caption = Once a conversation is over, a small model reads it in the background. No one waits.
dg-consolidation-talk = The conversation
dg-consolidation-silence = Then silence
dg-consolidation-silence-note = Longer than every medium of the address allows: a question asked aloud may get a typed answer for four hours.
dg-consolidation-model = A small model reads it
dg-consolidation-model-note = The consolidation model, the background one by default. It knows what is already remembered.
dg-consolidation-episode = An episode
dg-consolidation-episode-note = Two or three sentences and a few topics, for its participants. None if nothing is worth recalling.
dg-consolidation-facts = Facts
dg-consolidation-facts-note = Lasting facts the agent missed, kept as memories.
dg-consolidation-journal = The summary, journaled

dg-initiative-caption = How Nestor speaks first. The courier picks the place and medium and journals why, then the agent words the message.
dg-initiative-triggers = What calls for it
dg-initiative-schedule = A wake-up is due
dg-initiative-watch = A watch matches
dg-initiative-task = A task ends
dg-initiative-message = A message to pass on
dg-initiative-courier = The courier
dg-initiative-courier-note = The person's choice, who is home and where, quiet hours, urgency.
dg-initiative-agent = The agent words it
dg-initiative-agent-note = For that place and medium, knowing the conversation open there.
dg-initiative-arrives = How it arrives
dg-initiative-spoken = Said in the room
dg-initiative-spoken-note = By the satellite where the person is.
dg-initiative-written = Written where they read
dg-initiative-written-note = When they are away, asked for writing, or in quiet hours.
dg-initiative-followup = Then in writing
dg-initiative-followup-note = When nobody reacts to a spoken message.

## Satellites: pairing, the link, audio (PairingFlow)
dg-pairing-caption = A device pairs once, with whichever proof comes first, then keeps one link for everything. Ember crosses the network; dashed is audio, only when it is allowed.
dg-pairing-device = Device
dg-pairing-device-note = A speaker, a screen, a robot.
dg-pairing-core = Core
dg-pairing-core-note = The Nestor server, port 8471.
dg-pairing-person = Household member
dg-pairing-person-note = In the admin.
dg-pairing-from-to = { $from } → { $to }
dg-pairing-phase-pair = { $n } · Pairing
dg-pairing-phase-link = { $n } · The link
dg-pairing-phase-audio = { $n } · Audio, when allowed
dg-pairing-or = or, the first proof accepted wins
dg-pairing-request = Asks to pair
dg-pairing-request-note = With its manifest. It gets a pairing id and a device code.
dg-pairing-present = Presents its device code
dg-pairing-present-note = On its screen, aloud, or in its log.
dg-pairing-type = Types the device code
dg-pairing-type-note = The admin lists the devices waiting.
dg-pairing-give = Gives it an enrollment code
dg-pairing-give-note = Made in the admin: typed, provisioned, or shown as a QR code.
dg-pairing-enroll = Presents the enrollment code
dg-pairing-enroll-note = Or sends it with its first request, and is approved at once.
dg-pairing-token = Approved: the token, once
dg-pairing-token-note = The device asks until the pairing is decided.
dg-pairing-hello = Opens the link
dg-pairing-hello-note = hello with the token; welcome says what is allowed.
dg-pairing-exchange = Text, intents and acks, observations
dg-pairing-exchange-note = Both ways, over the same WebSocket.
dg-pairing-audio = Negotiates audio
dg-pairing-audio-note = A WebRTC offer with the token. That connection carries audio only.

## Satellites: the states of a pairing (PairingStates)
dg-states-caption = A pairing waits for one proof, hands out its token once, and expires if a deadline passes first. Ember is the way to a token.
dg-states-without = a request without a code
dg-states-proof = a proof accepted
dg-states-or = or
dg-states-enrolled = a request with an enrollment code
dg-states-claim = first poll: the token
dg-states-pending = Waits for a proof, 10 minutes.
dg-states-approved = The token waits for its first poll.
dg-states-claimed = The device holds its token. Later polls read claimed.
dg-states-expired = What an unknown id reads too.
dg-states-from-to = { $from } → { $to }
dg-states-late-pending = The deadline passes, or the device asks again.
dg-states-late-approved = The deadline passes, token unclaimed.
